    {
      "title": "FAA administrator urges ‘lay off’ Sean Duffy for the flight stoppage: ‘Blame me’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/faa-sean-duffy-flight-stoppage",
      "description": "<p>The comments come as the top US transportation official faces scrutiny over his handling of the tech outage crisis</p><p>The head of the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) took responsibility for <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/faa-nationwide-ground-stop-flights\">the nationwide ground stop </a>that affected more than<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/14/faa-ground-stop-flights-resume-airport-chaos\"> 12,400 flights </a>on Friday, urging people to “lay off” <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/transportation-secretary-sean-duffy-faa-flight-stoppag\">Sean Duffy, the transportation secretary.</a></p><p>“I take full responsibility for it,” Bryan Bedford, the FAA administrator, said at an event featuring aviation officials and lawmakers on Wednesday,<a href=\"https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/18/faa-chief-blame-duffy-01172188\"> Politico reported.</a></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/faa-sean-duffy-flight-stoppage\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-18T19:14:38"
    },
    {
      "title": "FAA suspends installation of router that led to a ground stop of flights across the US",
